WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.330
Hi! How do verbs change for things that happened yesterday, or will happen tomorrow? Today we'll learn the simple past, past continuous and simple future.

2
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:19.482
For finished actions, use the simple past. Clue words: yesterday, last week, ago.

3
00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:23.466
Regular verbs add ed, like visited and played.

4
00:00:23.616 --> 00:00:30.714
Irregular verbs must be remembered: go becomes went, eat becomes ate, see becomes saw.

5
00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:38.778
Questions and negatives use did, followed by the base verb: Did you go? I did not go.

6
00:00:38.928 --> 00:00:45.570
The past continuous is for an action in progress in the past: was or were plus ing.

7
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:54.810
Mum was cooking, and the phone rang. The long action uses the past continuous, and the short one that interrupts it uses the simple past.

8
00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:03.378
The simple future is for things that haven't happened yet: will plus the base verb. Clue words: tomorrow, next week.

9
00:01:03.528 --> 00:01:10.170
The verb after will is always the base form: She will come, not will comes.

10
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:15.306
Watch out! With yesterday, the verb must be in the past tense!

11
00:01:15.456 --> 00:01:19.938
Go is irregular. Its past form is went, not goed.

12
00:01:20.088 --> 00:01:24.810
So we say: Yesterday I went to the park.

13
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:34.674
Your turn! Last Sunday, we, ___, a film. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:34.824 --> 00:01:40.818
Last Sunday is in the past, so watched. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:51.066
Another one! They, ___, football when it started to rain. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:51.216 --> 00:01:59.730
Playing football is the long action interrupted by the rain. They takes were playing. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:10.122
Here's another! Next week, Dad, ___, us to the beach. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:02:10.272 --> 00:02:16.050
Next week is the future, so will take. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:25.506
Try one more! Did you, ___, your homework? Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:25.656 --> 00:02:31.866
After did, use the base form: finish. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:32.016 --> 00:02:41.970
Last one! I, ___, a rainbow two days ago. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:49.290
Two days ago is past. The past form of see is saw. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:49.440 --> 00:03:01.818
Remember: use the past form for finished actions and learn the irregular ones. Use was or were plus ing for actions in progress in the past, and will plus the base verb for the future.

24
00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:07.650
Today, say what you did yesterday and what you will do tomorrow!

